C\\to B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065461/state.json" "file_sha256" "1bcf1521b865fb1acf6ed0120325be8fb604644d04ed78732d71304d5847c209"} {"question" "q-35795" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065461/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9033a7a857858aa2623b7114ae34d4374fd3f0a185272c6b9db507039da7f4f2"} {"question" "q-35795" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065461/state.json" "file_sha256" "1bcf1521b865fb1acf6ed0120325be8fb604644d04ed78732d71304d5847c209"} {"question" "q-35795" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 3\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065461/state.json" "file_sha256" "1bcf1521b865fb1acf6ed0120325be8fb604644d04ed78732d71304d5847c209"} {"question" "q-35795" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065461/state.json" "file_sha256" "1bcf1521b865fb1acf6ed0120325be8fb604644d04ed78732d71304d5847c209"} {"question" "q-81394" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}}$ and $C={{c}_{1},{c}_{2},{c}_{3}}$ be bases of ${R}^{3}.$ \nWhat are the values of $a,b,$ and $c$ if \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1} & ={c}_{1}+2{c}_{2}-{c}_{3}, \\\\ {b}_{2} & =5{c}_{3}+2{c}_{2}, \\\\ {b}_{3} & ={c}_{2}-{c}_{1},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand  the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C$ is\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to C}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ a & b & 1 \\\\ -1 & c & 0\\end{aligned}]?\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065461/state.json" "file_sha256" "1bcf1521b865fb1acf6ed0120325be8fb604644d04ed78732d71304d5847c209"} {"question" "q-81394" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The coordinates of the vectors in $B$ relative to the basis $C$ are\n\n$$\n[{b}_{1}]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,[{b}_{2}]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],\\,[{b}_{3}]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C$ is a matrix whose respective columns are the coordinates of the vectors of $B$ relative to the basis $C.$ \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to C}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 5 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, $a=2,$ $b=2,$ and $c=5.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065461/state.json" "file_sha256" "1bcf1521b865fb1acf6ed0120325be8fb604644d04ed78732d71304d5847c209"} {"question" "q-81394" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065461/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9033a7a857858aa2623b7114ae34d4374fd3f0a185272c6b9db507039da7f4f2"} {"question" "q-81394" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065461/state.json" "file_sha256" "1bcf1521b865fb1acf6ed0120325be8fb604644d04ed78732d71304d5847c209"} {"question" "q-81394" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$a=0,$ $b=2,$ and $c=-1$"] ["text" "$a=1,$ $b=-2,$ and $c=5$"] ["text" "$a=1,$ $b=2,$ and $c=0$"] ["text" "$a=2,$ $b=0,$ and $c=-1$"] ["text" "$a=2,$ $b=2,$ and $c=5$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065461/state.json" "file_sha256" "1bcf1521b865fb1acf6ed0120325be8fb604644d04ed78732d71304d5847c209"} {"question" "q-81394" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$a=2,$ $b=2,$ and $c=5$"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065461/state.json" "file_sha256" "1bcf1521b865fb1acf6ed0120325be8fb604644d04ed78732d71304d5847c209"} {"question" "q-36366" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ be a basis of ${R}^{2}$ and let $S$ be the standard basis of ${R}^{2}.$ \nFind the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{B\\to S}$ from $B$ to $S$ if \n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065461/state.json" "file_sha256" "1bcf1521b865fb1acf6ed0120325be8fb604644d04ed78732d71304d5847c209"} {"question" "q-36366" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall  that the standard basis of ${R}^{2}$ consists of the vectors ${e}_{1}$ and ${e}_{2},$ given by\n\n$$\n{e}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{e}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe components of the vectors of $B$ are just the coordinates relative to the standard basis:\n\n$$\n[{b}_{1}]_{S}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,[{b}_{2}]_{S}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $S$ is a matrix whose respective columns are the coordinates of the vectors of $B$ relative to the basis $S.$ \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to S}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065461/state.json" "file_sha256" "1bcf1521b865fb1acf6ed0120325be8fb604644d04ed78732d71304d5847c209"} {"question" "q-36366" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065461/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9033a7a857858aa2623b7114ae34d4374fd3f0a185272c6b9db507039da7f4f2"} {"question" "q-36366" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065461/state.json" "file_sha256" "1bcf1521b865fb1acf6ed0120325be8fb604644d04ed78732d71304d5847c209"} {"question" "q-36366" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -3 & -2\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065461/state.json" "file_sha256" "1bcf1521b865fb1acf6ed0120325be8fb604644d04ed78732d71304d5847c209"} {"question" "q-36366" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065461/state.json" "file_sha256" "1bcf1521b865fb1acf6ed0120325be8fb604644d04ed78732d71304d5847c209"} {"question" "q-36401" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ be a basis of ${R}^{2}$ and let $S$ be the standard basis of ${R}^{2}.$ \nFind the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{B\\to S}$ from $B$ to $S$ if \n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065461/state.json" "file_sha256" "1bcf1521b865fb1acf6ed0120325be8fb604644d04ed78732d71304d5847c209"} {"question" "q-36401" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall  that the standard basis of ${R}^{2}$ consists of the vectors ${e}_{1}$ and ${e}_{2},$ given by\n\n$$\n{e}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{e}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe components of the vectors of $B$ are just the coordinates relative to the standard basis:\n\n$$\n[{b}_{1}]_{S}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,[{b}_{2}]_{S}=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $S$ is a matrix whose respective columns are the coordinates of the vectors of $B$ relative to the basis $S.$ \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to S}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 7 \\\\ -3 & -4\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065461/state.json" "file_sha256" "1bcf1521b865fb1acf